   "q_no": 3,
   "topic": "Laws of Motion",
   "qtype": "mcq",
   "section": "Category 1",
   "stem": "The minimum force required to start pushing a body up a rough (having co-efficient of friction $\\mu$) inclined plane is $\\vec{F_1}$ while the minimum force needed to prevent it from sliding is $\\vec{F_2}$. If the inclined plane makes an angle $\\theta$ with the horizontal such that $\\tan\\theta = 2\\mu$, then the ratio $F_1/F_2$ is",
